    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. It seems like they basically just mirror the power dynamics that already exist instead of actually providing a fair framework. Beyond the veto power, are there other ways these global institutions end up undermining a country's ability to govern itself? Like, do you see any systematic ways they force specific economic or social policies on nations that don't want them?",
